  "result": "Fixed. Completion now handles arguments containing `#` correctly.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex.shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment character by default. Everything after a `#` was silently dropped, so `cli a#b c` was parsed as `[\"cli\", \"a\"]`.\n\n**Fix:** set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is an ordinary character.\n\n**Tests:** I added `a#b` and `#tag` cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`. The parser and shell completion tests pass (67 passed).",
